<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The launcher icon for API 24 and 25, which have no adaptive icons and apply no
  mask: whatever this draws is what the home screen shows, corners and all.

  So it is not the adaptive pair stacked. It is the same composition **already
  cropped** — the mesh and the monogram both scaled 1.5x about the centre, which
  is exactly the 72dp of a 108dp adaptive icon that a launcher mask leaves
  visible — and then clipped to a rounded square itself. Stack the adaptive layers
  instead and Android 7 gets a square with a 57dp mark adrift in the middle of
  it, ringed by 25dp of empty ground on every side.

  The 24dp corner radius is the pre-Oreo convention — near enough to what
  Android 7's own launcher rounds a bitmap icon to that this does not read as the
  one square icon in the tray.

  Kept in step with `ic_launcher_background.xml` and `ic_launcher_foreground.xml`
  by hand. If the mesh or the mark moves there, the 1.5x copies here move too;
  there is no way to share geometry between vector drawables.
-->
